<.shell current={:build_a_group_rule}>
  <h1>Build a group rule</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    An editor inside a page: small inputs and small buttons, since it sits among other content.
  </p>

  <div class="example measure">
    <p class="card">{rule_sentence(rule_sentence_rules())}</p>
    <.rule_editor rows={rule_rows()} options={rule_options()} new_path="#" />
  </div>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      The rules are a <a href={page_path(:table)}>table</a>. A member must meet every one to be in the
      group.
    </li>
    <li>
      An In rule is met by being in any of its groups or holding any of its endorsements. A Not in
      rule is met by none of them. A Standing is rule is met by any of its standings: Active, Away,
      or Not a person.
    </li>
    <li>
      A group with rules but no Standing is rule gets a suggestion, Standing is Active, with a button
      to add it. It is never added for you.
    </li>
    <li>
      Above the editor, the rules read as one sentence, with every group and endorsement in bold.
    </li>
    <li>
      Each rule links to its own page, where its groups and endorsements change. The menu adds a
      rule with one. Its second menu follows the first: groups and endorsements for In and Not in,
      standings for Standing is. New endorsement makes an endorsement and adds it as an In rule.
    </li>
    <li>Done closes the editor. Members change only after you review and send the changes.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="spec">
    <code>&lt;.rule_editor rows=&#123;…&#125; options=&#123;…&#125; new_path=&#123;…&#125; /&gt;</code>
    and <code>rule_sentence/1</code>
    from <code>Web.Components.GroupRule</code>, as on a group's page, with made-up groups.
  </p>
</.shell>
